Analytics DE external keys (Survey Results):
sst_analytics_answers
sst_analytics_per_course (LookupRows/DeleteData by surveyId)

SST_SP_Survey_Responses_DE — TextPageNumber batch (text only, 20 rows = 1 UI page)

Survey Results (CloudPage):
- View all + preview use LookupOrderedRows (20-row window by LastUpdated ASC). TextPageNumber is for batch/QA only until LookupRows is re-enabled after DE is on the CloudPage collection.

Do not use legacy PageNumber for text UI; keep TextPageNumber separate from any other PageNumber job.

Incremental batch (new text rows only, TextPageNumber IS NULL). Output feeds update on ResponsePK.

SELECT
    n.ResponsePK,
    CAST(
        (ISNULL(pc.ExistingCount, 0) + n.NewRowNum - 1) / 20 + 1
    AS INT) AS TextPageNumber,
    n.Contact,
    n.SurveyID,
    n.QuestionID,
    n.QuestionNumber,
    n.QuestionText,
    n.QuestionType,
    n.Response,
    n.Status,
    n.LastUpdated,
    n.CourseName
FROM (
    SELECT
        ResponsePK,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY SurveyID, QuestionID
            ORDER BY LastUpdated ASC, ResponsePK
        ) AS NewRowNum,
        Contact,
        SurveyID,
        QuestionID,
        QuestionNumber,
        QuestionText,
        QuestionType,
        Response,
        Status,
        LastUpdated,
        CourseName
    FROM SST_SP_Survey_Responses_DE
    WHERE TextPageNumber IS NULL
      AND QuestionType = 'text'
      AND Response IS NOT NULL
      AND LTRIM(RTRIM(Response)) <> ''
) n
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT
        SurveyID,
        QuestionID,
        COUNT(1) AS ExistingCount
    FROM SST_SP_Survey_Responses_DE
    WHERE TextPageNumber IS NOT NULL
      AND QuestionType = 'text'
    GROUP BY SurveyID, QuestionID
) pc
    ON pc.SurveyID = n.SurveyID
   AND pc.QuestionID = n.QuestionID

After changing batch logic, clear TextPageNumber on affected text rows and re-batch, or run a one-time full renumber for text questions.

CloudPage collection must include SST_SP_Survey_Responses_DE with TextPageNumber indexed if lookups are slow (optional SFMC tuning).
